  "description": "Application under Section 73 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 to carry out development without compliance with Condition 1 (Approved Drawings) of planning permission 25/01215/FUL (Erection of a single storey rear extension, hip-to-gable roof conversion with rear dormer  and installation 2nos front rooflights. Conversion of a single dwelling house into two self-contained flats) to increase the size of rear extension.\r",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant has failed to demonstrate through the submission of cogent information that the proposed rear extension would not have an unacceptable adverse impact on the closest habitable room windows at No. 151 Tolworth Rise North in terms of daylight/sunlight. Given the scale of the extension and the proximity of neighbouring windows it is considered that there is a likelihood that the development would breach the \"BRE 45 Degree Rule\" and reduce light entering into the neighbouring habitable room, which in turn would harm the residential amenities of the occupants of the neighbouring property.  The proposal is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
